segments.text:
Secondly, they teach that their Preists appointed to be comforters and releeuers of the distressed, are made by Christ himselfe
iudges of the Cases of conscience, hauing in their owne hands a iudicarie po•…er and authoritie, truly and properly to binde or to loose, to remitte or to retaine sinnes, to open or to shut the kingdome of heauen. Whereas the Scripture vttereth a contrarie voice, that Christ onely hath the keyes of Dauid, which properly and truly openeth, and no man shutteth, and properly and truly shutteth, and no man openeth. And the Ministers of God are not called to be absolute Iudges of the Consciēce, but onely Messengers and Embassado•rs of reconciliation;
wherevpon it followeth, that they cannot be the authors and gi•ers of remission of sinnes, but onely the Ministers and Dispensers of the same.
